export default {"T001300":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"implies\" data-relation-style=\"implication\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Implication</span><h3>Quasi-compact immersion ⇒ Separated and quasi-finite</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All premises</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000549\"><span>Quasi-compact immersion</span><code>P000549</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../database/#T001300\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">T001300</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">⇒</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All conclusions</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000555\"><span>Separated and quasi-finite</span><code>P000555</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Morphisms of schemes</p><p><strong>Justification.</strong> An immersion is locally quasi-finite and a monomorphism. Quasi-compactness gives quasi-finiteness, and monomorphisms are separated.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01TN\">Stacks 01TN · immersions are locally quasi-finite</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/morphisms/#tag-01TN\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02NH\">Stacks 02NH · finite fibres and quasi-finiteness</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/morphisms/#tag-02NH\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01L7\">Stacks 01L7 · immersions are monomorphisms</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/schemes/#tag-01L7\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01L4\">Stacks 01L4 · monomorphisms are separated</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/schemes/#tag-01L4\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://link.springer.com/content/pdf/10.1007/978-3-658-30733-2_13.pdf#page=8\">Görtz &amp; Wedhorn, Algebraic Geometry I: Schemes, 2nd ed., Proposition 12.17(1), p. 331. A quasi-compact immersion is quasi-finite.</a> · <a href=\"https://link.springer.com/content/pdf/10.1007/978-3-658-30733-2_10.pdf#page=5\">Görtz &amp; Wedhorn, Algebraic Geometry I: Schemes, 2nd ed., Proposition 9.13(1), p. 234. Every monomorphism, in particular every immersion, is separated.</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#T001300\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../database/#T001300\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>","T001301":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"implies\" data-relation-style=\"implication\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Implication</span><h3>Immersion ⇒ Monomorphism</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All premises</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000548\"><span>Immersion</span><code>P000548</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../database/#T001301\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">T001301</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">⇒</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All conclusions</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000550\"><span>Monomorphism</span><code>P000550</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Morphisms of schemes</p><p><strong>Justification.</strong> Apply the monomorphism criterion to the open and closed factors.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01L7\">Stacks 01L7 · immersions are monomorphisms</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/schemes/#tag-01L7\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#T001301\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../database/#T001301\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>","T001302":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"implies\" data-relation-style=\"implication\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Implication</span><h3>Monomorphism ⇒ Universally injective</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All premises</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000550\"><span>Monomorphism</span><code>P000550</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../database/#T001302\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">T001302</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">⇒</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All conclusions</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000044\"><span>Universally injective</span><code>P000044</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Morphisms of schemes</p><p><strong>Justification.</strong> The diagonal is an isomorphism, so it is surjective. Surjectivity of the diagonal characterizes universal injectivity.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01L3\">Stacks 01L3 · monomorphism criterion</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/schemes/#tag-01L3\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01S4\">Stacks 01S4 · universal injectivity criterion</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/morphisms/#tag-01S4\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#T001302\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../database/#T001302\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>","T001303":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"implies\" data-relation-style=\"implication\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Implication</span><h3>Universally injective ⇒ Separated</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All premises</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000044\"><span>Universally injective</span><code>P000044</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../database/#T001303\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">T001303</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">⇒</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All conclusions</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000024\"><span>Separated</span><code>P000024</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Morphisms of schemes</p><p><strong>Justification.</strong> The diagonal is a surjective immersion and hence a closed immersion.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05VE\">Stacks 05VE · universally injective morphisms are separated</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/morphisms/#tag-05VE\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#T001303\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../database/#T001303\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>","T001304":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"implies\" data-relation-style=\"implication\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Implication</span><h3>Étale ⇒ Smooth</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All premises</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000003\"><span>Étale</span><code>P000003</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../database/#T001304\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">T001304</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">⇒</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All conclusions</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000004\"><span>Smooth</span><code>P000004</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Morphisms of schemes</p><p><strong>Justification.</strong> Étale morphisms are smooth of relative dimension zero.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02GK\">Stacks 02GK · étale iff smooth and unramified</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/morphisms/#tag-02GK\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#T001304\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../database/#T001304\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>","T001305":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"implies\" data-relation-style=\"implication\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Implication</span><h3>Smooth ⇒ Flat ∧ locally finitely presented</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All premises</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000004\"><span>Smooth</span><code>P000004</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../database/#T001305\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">T001305</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">⇒</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All conclusions</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000039\"><span>Flat ∧ locally finitely presented</span><code>P000039</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Morphisms of schemes</p><p><strong>Justification.</strong> Smooth morphisms are flat and locally of finite presentation.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01VF\">Stacks 01VF · flatness of smooth morphisms</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/morphisms/#tag-01VF\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01VE\">Stacks 01VE · local finite presentation of smooth morphisms</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/morphisms/#tag-01VE\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#T001305\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../database/#T001305\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>","T001306":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"implies\" data-relation-style=\"implication\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Implication</span><h3>Faithfully flat and qc ⇒ Universally submersive</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All premises</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000552\"><span>Faithfully flat and qc</span><code>P000552</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../database/#T001306\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">T001306</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">⇒</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All conclusions</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000553\"><span>Universally submersive</span><code>P000553</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Morphisms of schemes</p><p><strong>Justification.</strong> The hypotheses survive arbitrary base change. The quotient-topology lemma applies to each base-changed morphism.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02JY\">Stacks 02JY · flat quasi-compact surjections are submersive</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/morphisms/#tag-02JY\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01U9\">Stacks 01U9 · flat base change</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/morphisms/#tag-01U9\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01S1\">Stacks 01S1 · surjectivity under base change</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/morphisms/#tag-01S1\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01K5\">Stacks 01K5 · quasi-compactness under base change</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/schemes/#tag-01K5\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#T001306\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../database/#T001306\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>","T001307":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"implies\" data-relation-style=\"implication\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Implication</span><h3>Universally submersive ⇒ Surjective</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All premises</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000553\"><span>Universally submersive</span><code>P000553</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../database/#T001307\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">T001307</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">⇒</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All conclusions</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000043\"><span>Surjective</span><code>P000043</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Morphisms of schemes</p><p><strong>Justification.</strong> Apply the quotient-map condition to the identity base change.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/040H\">Stacks 040H · universal submersiveness</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/morphisms/#tag-040H\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#T001307\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../database/#T001307\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>","T001308":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"equivalence\" data-relation-style=\"equivalence\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Equivalence</span><h3>Universal homeomorphism of finite type ⇔ Finite ∧ Universally injective ∧ Surjective</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">Left conditions (all)</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000554\"><span>Universal homeomorphism of finite type</span><code>P000554</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../database/#T001308\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">T001308</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">⇔</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">Right conditions (all)</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000019\"><span>Finite</span><code>P000019</code></a><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000044\"><span>Universally injective</span><code>P000044</code></a><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000043\"><span>Surjective</span><code>P000043</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Morphisms of schemes</p><p><strong>Justification.</strong> Universal homeomorphisms are integral, surjective and universally injective. An integral morphism of finite type is finite. Conversely a finite morphism is integral, and adding surjectivity and universal injectivity gives a universal homeomorphism of finite type.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/04DF\">Stacks 04DF · characterization of universal homeomorphisms</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/morphisms/#tag-04DF\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01WJ\">Stacks 01WJ · finite and integral morphisms</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/morphisms/#tag-01WJ\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01WN\">Stacks 01WN · finite implies proper, hence finite type</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/morphisms/#tag-01WN\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#T001308\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../database/#T001308\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>","T001309":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"implies\" data-relation-style=\"implication\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Implication</span><h3>Universal homeomorphism ⇒ Universally open</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All premises</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000041\"><span>Universal homeomorphism</span><code>P000041</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../database/#T001309\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">T001309</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">⇒</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All conclusions</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000040\"><span>Universally open</span><code>P000040</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Morphisms of schemes</p><p><strong>Justification.</strong> A homeomorphism maps opens to opens, after any base change.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/04DD\">Stacks 04DD · universal homeomorphisms</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/morphisms/#tag-04DD\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#T001309\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../database/#T001309\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>","T001310":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"implies\" data-relation-style=\"implication\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Implication</span><h3>Universal homeomorphism ⇒ Universally submersive</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All premises</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000041\"><span>Universal homeomorphism</span><code>P000041</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../database/#T001310\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">T001310</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">⇒</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All conclusions</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000553\"><span>Universally submersive</span><code>P000553</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Morphisms of schemes</p><p><strong>Justification.</strong> A homeomorphism is a quotient map, after any base change.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/04DD\">Stacks 04DD · universal homeomorphisms</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/morphisms/#tag-04DD\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/040H\">Stacks 040H · universal submersiveness</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/morphisms/#tag-040H\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#T001310\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../database/#T001310\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>","T001311":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"implies\" data-relation-style=\"implication\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Implication</span><h3>Finite ⇒ Separated and quasi-finite</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All premises</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000019\"><span>Finite</span><code>P000019</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../database/#T001311\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">T001311</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">⇒</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All conclusions</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000555\"><span>Separated and quasi-finite</span><code>P000555</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Morphisms of schemes</p><p><strong>Justification.</strong> A finite morphism is quasi-finite and separated.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02NU\">Stacks 02NU · finite implies quasi-finite</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/morphisms/#tag-02NU\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01WN\">Stacks 01WN · finite implies proper</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/morphisms/#tag-01WN\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#T001311\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../database/#T001311\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>","T001312":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"equivalence\" data-relation-style=\"equivalence\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Equivalence</span><h3>Finite ⇔ Quasi-affine ∧ Proper</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">Left conditions (all)</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000019\"><span>Finite</span><code>P000019</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../database/#T001312\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">T001312</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">⇔</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">Right conditions (all)</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000018\"><span>Quasi-affine</span><code>P000018</code></a><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000023\"><span>Proper</span><code>P000023</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Morphisms of schemes</p><p><strong>Justification.</strong> For the converse, the structure sheaf of a quasi-affine morphism is relatively ample. Apply the universally closed ampleness lemma with section 1 to obtain affineness. Affine and proper is equivalent to finite.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0891\">Stacks 0891 · relative ampleness of the structure sheaf</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/morphisms/#tag-0891\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EKE\">Stacks 0EKE · affine nonvanishing locus over a universally closed map</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/morphisms/#tag-0EKE\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01WN\">Stacks 01WN · finite iff affine and proper</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/morphisms/#tag-01WN\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01SP\">Stacks 01SP · affine implies quasi-affine</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/morphisms/#tag-01SP\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#T001312\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../database/#T001312\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>","T001313":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"equivalence\" data-relation-style=\"equivalence\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Equivalence</span><h3>Integral morphism ⇔ Affine ∧ Universally closed</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">Left conditions (all)</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000045\"><span>Integral morphism</span><code>P000045</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../database/#T001313\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">T001313</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">⇔</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">Right conditions (all)</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000017\"><span>Affine</span><code>P000017</code></a><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000042\"><span>Universally closed</span><code>P000042</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Morphisms of schemes</p><p><strong>Justification.</strong> The cited lemma gives both directions, with no finiteness hypothesis.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01WM\">Stacks 01WM · integral iff affine and universally closed</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/morphisms/#tag-01WM\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#T001313\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../database/#T001313\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>","T001314":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"implies\" data-relation-style=\"implication\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Implication</span><h3>Separated and quasi-finite ⇒ Quasi-affine of finite type</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All premises</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000555\"><span>Separated and quasi-finite</span><code>P000555</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../database/#T001314\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">T001314</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">⇒</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All conclusions</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000556\"><span>Quasi-affine of finite type</span><code>P000556</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Morphisms of schemes</p><p><strong>Justification.</strong> Zariski’s Main Theorem factors the map through a quasi-compact open immersion into a scheme integral over the target. Quasi-finiteness supplies finite type.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02LR\">Stacks 02LR · separated quasi-finite morphisms are quasi-affine</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/more-morphisms/#tag-02LR\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02NH\">Stacks 02NH · finite fibres and quasi-finiteness</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/morphisms/#tag-02NH\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://link.springer.com/content/pdf/10.1007/978-3-658-30733-2_13.pdf#page=41\">Görtz &amp; Wedhorn, Algebraic Geometry I: Schemes, 2nd ed., Corollary 12.91, p. 364. For a separated quasi-finite morphism, the canonical map to the relative spectrum of its direct-image structure sheaf is a quasi-compact open immersion.</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#T001314\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../database/#T001314\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>","T001315":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"implies\" data-relation-style=\"implication\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Implication</span><h3>Quasi-affine of finite type ⇒ Quasi-projective</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All premises</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000556\"><span>Quasi-affine of finite type</span><code>P000556</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../database/#T001315\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">T001315</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">⇒</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All conclusions</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000021\"><span>Quasi-projective</span><code>P000021</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Morphisms of schemes</p><p><strong>Justification.</strong> The structure sheaf is relatively ample and the morphism is of finite type.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B3H\">Stacks 0B3H · quasi-affine of finite type implies quasi-projective</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/morphisms/#tag-0B3H\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#T001315\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../database/#T001315\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>","T001316":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"implies\" data-relation-style=\"implication\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Implication</span><h3>Projective ⇒ Proper and quasi-projective</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All premises</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000020\"><span>Projective</span><code>P000020</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../database/#T001316\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">T001316</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">⇒</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All conclusions</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000557\"><span>Proper and quasi-projective</span><code>P000557</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Morphisms of schemes</p><p><strong>Justification.</strong> Projectivity implies both properness and quasi-projectivity over any target.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01WC\">Stacks 01WC · locally projective implies proper</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/morphisms/#tag-01WC\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07RL\">Stacks 07RL · projective implies quasi-projective</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/morphisms/#tag-07RL\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#T001316\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../database/#T001316\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>","T001317":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"implies\" data-relation-style=\"implication\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Implication</span><h3>Proper and quasi-projective ∧ Qcqs target ⇒ Projective</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All premises</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000557\"><span>Proper and quasi-projective</span><code>P000557</code></a><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000470\"><span>Qcqs target</span><code>P000470</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../database/#T001317\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">T001317</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">⇒</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All conclusions</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000020\"><span>Projective</span><code>P000020</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Morphisms of schemes</p><p><strong>Justification.</strong> Over a qcqs target, quasi-projectivity gives an open immersion into a projective scheme over the target. Properness makes this immersion closed.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BCL\">Stacks 0BCL · projectivity over a qcqs target</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/morphisms/#tag-0BCL\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#T001317\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../database/#T001317\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>","T001318":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"implies\" data-relation-style=\"implication\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Implication</span><h3>Quasi-affine ⇒ Separated and qc</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All premises</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000018\"><span>Quasi-affine</span><code>P000018</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../database/#T001318\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">T001318</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">⇒</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All conclusions</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000558\"><span>Separated and qc</span><code>P000558</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Morphisms of schemes</p><p><strong>Justification.</strong> Over affine opens of the target the inverse images are quasi-compact open subschemes of affine schemes.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01SL\">Stacks 01SL · quasi-affine implies separated and quasi-compact</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/morphisms/#tag-01SL\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#T001318\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../database/#T001318\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>","T001319":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"implies\" data-relation-style=\"implication\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Implication</span><h3>Proper ⇒ Separated and qc</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All premises</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000023\"><span>Proper</span><code>P000023</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../database/#T001319\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">T001319</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">⇒</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All conclusions</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000558\"><span>Separated and qc</span><code>P000558</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Morphisms of schemes</p><p><strong>Justification.</strong> Properness includes separatedness and finite type. Finite type includes quasi-compactness.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01W1\">Stacks 01W1 · properness</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/morphisms/#tag-01W1\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01T1\">Stacks 01T1 · finite type</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/morphisms/#tag-01T1\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#T001319\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../database/#T001319\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>","T001320":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"implies\" data-relation-style=\"implication\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Implication</span><h3>Quasi-projective ⇒ Separated and qc</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All premises</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000021\"><span>Quasi-projective</span><code>P000021</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../database/#T001320\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">T001320</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">⇒</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All conclusions</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000558\"><span>Separated and qc</span><code>P000558</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Morphisms of schemes</p><p><strong>Justification.</strong> Quasi-projectivity implies separatedness and finite type, hence quasi-compactness.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01VX\">Stacks 01VX · quasi-projective implies separated and of finite type</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/morphisms/#tag-01VX\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01T1\">Stacks 01T1 · finite type</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/morphisms/#tag-01T1\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#T001320\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../database/#T001320\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>","T001321":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"implies\" data-relation-style=\"implication\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Implication</span><h3>Quasi-projective ⇒ Of finite type</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All premises</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000021\"><span>Quasi-projective</span><code>P000021</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../database/#T001321\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">T001321</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">⇒</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All conclusions</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000026\"><span>Of finite type</span><code>P000026</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Morphisms of schemes</p><p><strong>Justification.</strong> Finite type is included in the definition of quasi-projectivity used here.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01VW\">Stacks 01VW · quasi-projectivity</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/morphisms/#tag-01VW\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01VX\">Stacks 01VX · quasi-projective implies separated and of finite type</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/morphisms/#tag-01VX\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#T001321\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../database/#T001321\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>","T001322":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"implies\" data-relation-style=\"implication\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Implication</span><h3>Separated and qc ⇒ Qcqs morphism</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All premises</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000558\"><span>Separated and qc</span><code>P000558</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../database/#T001322\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">T001322</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">⇒</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All conclusions</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000047\"><span>Qcqs morphism</span><code>P000047</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Morphisms of schemes</p><p><strong>Justification.</strong> The diagonal is a closed immersion, hence quasi-compact.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01KK\">Stacks 01KK · separatedness and quasi-separatedness</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/schemes/#tag-01KK\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01K7\">Stacks 01K7 · closed immersions are quasi-compact</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/schemes/#tag-01K7\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#T001322\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../database/#T001322\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>","T001323":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"implies\" data-relation-style=\"implication\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Implication</span><h3>Of finite type ⇒ Quasi-compact</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All premises</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000026\"><span>Of finite type</span><code>P000026</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../database/#T001323\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">T001323</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">⇒</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All conclusions</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000022\"><span>Quasi-compact</span><code>P000022</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Morphisms of schemes</p><p><strong>Justification.</strong> Finite type includes quasi-compactness.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01T1\">Stacks 01T1 · finite type</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/morphisms/#tag-01T1\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#T001323\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../database/#T001323\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>","T001324":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"implies\" data-relation-style=\"implication\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Implication</span><h3>Of finite presentation ⇒ Qcqs morphism</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All premises</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000027\"><span>Of finite presentation</span><code>P000027</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../database/#T001324\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">T001324</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">⇒</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">All conclusions</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000047\"><span>Qcqs morphism</span><code>P000047</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Morphisms of schemes</p><p><strong>Justification.</strong> Finite presentation includes quasi-compactness and quasi-separatedness.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01TY\">Stacks 01TY · finite presentation implies qcqs</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/morphisms/#tag-01TY\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#T001324\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../database/#T001324\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>","T001325":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"equivalence\" data-relation-style=\"equivalence\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Equivalence</span><h3>Nonempty space ∧ Connected space (Pi-Base convention) ⇔ Connected space (Stacks convention)</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">Left conditions (all)</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000561\"><span>Nonempty space</span><code>P000561</code></a><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000060\"><span>Connected space (Pi-Base convention)</span><code>P000060</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../database/#T001325\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">T001325</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">⇔</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">Right conditions (all)</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000562\"><span>Connected space (Stacks convention)</span><code>P000562</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Topological spaces</p><p><strong>Justification.</strong> The two factors give exactly the Stacks definition.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/004S\">Stacks 004S · connectedness and components</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../database/stacks/topology/#tag-004S\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://topology.pi-base.org/properties/P000036\">Pi-Base connectedness</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#T001325\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../database/#T001325\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>"};
